   "page": 1,
   "source": "layout-regroup",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "text": "‘Abacus’ is intended for sowing in autumn and winter in the\nlonger season, wetter areas (600-1000 mm annual rainfall) of\nthe southern wheat belt. ‘Abacus’ has been observed to be tol-\nerant of acid soil, and shows field resistance to stem, leaf and\nstripe rusts (Puccinia graminis, P. recondita and P. striiformis).",
