   "id": "r18",
   "page": 1,
   "source": "layout-regroup",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "text": "“Taranna’ is a new variety of the native grass Danthonia\nrichardsonii. \\t is distinct from the only other known variety\n‘Hume’ in having a wider inflorescence and glumes, longer\nflag leaves and wider flag and tiller leaves. Although the culm\nheights of the two varieties are similar, “Taranna’ has a greater\ninternodal distance between the first and second nodes on the\nculm. At flowering the leaves of ‘Taranna’ tend to be a darker\ncolour than those of ‘Hume’.",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
